.TH EUCLID-CLI-EDS-LIST-RECORDS 1 "November 2026" "euclid-cli 2.3.2" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eds-list-records \- list a zone's record sets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eds list-records
.BR \-\-zone | \-z
.I ZONE
[\fB\-\-name\fR|\fB\-n\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-type\fR|\fB\-t\fR \fITYPE\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-size\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-index\fR \fIN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists the record sets stored in a zone, ordered by name and then by
type, with their values exactly as they were put.
.PP
The zone's SOA and its default NS are not listed: they are made from the
zone rather than stored. To see them as the server answers them, use
.BR euclid-cli-eds-get-answer (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-zone " " \fIZONE\fR
The zone's apex. Required.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Only the sets at this name, written as for
.BR euclid-cli-eds-put-record (1).
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-type " " \fITYPE\fR
Only the sets of this type.
.TP
.BR \-\-page\-size " " \fIN\fR
Most sets to return. Without it, all of them.
.TP
.BR \-\-page\-index " " \fIN\fR
Zero-based page, used with
.BR \-\-page\-size .
.SH OUTPUT
A JSON object:
.I records
\- each with
.IR zone ,
.IR name ,
.IR type ,
.I ttl
(0 meaning the zone's),
.IR values ,
.I created
and
.I modified
\- and
.IR total ,
the number of sets matching the filters.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The records were listed, possibly none.
.TP
.B 1
No such zone in your account, a name outside the zone, an unknown type,
or a grant does not allow reading the zone.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli eds list-records --zone corp.example
euclid-cli eds list-records --zone corp.example --type A \e
    | jq -r '.records[] | "\e(.name) \e(.values | join(" "))"'
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eds (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eds-update-record (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eds-put-record (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eds-delete-record (1)
